Translation patch: keystore2::legacy_blob::LegacyBlobLoader::make_blob_filename

Change: keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs:942, 944: each `format!` on these lines is replaced, on the same line, by a block that builds the same `String` with `to_owned`, `push_str` and `to_string`: the string `{prefix}_{alias}` that is encoded, and the file name `{uid}_{encoded_alias}`, are built from their parts.
Why: the translation models the arguments of `format!` as `()` (`core::fmt::Arguments` is `Unit` in the Aeneas library), so the translated function gave the same file name for every prefix, alias and uid. `to_owned`, `push_str` and `to_string` are translated as calls whose results depend on their arguments.
Behaviour: unchanged. The encoded string and the file name are the same. `Display` of a string or an integer with no format options writes the same bytes as `push_str` of the string or of the integer's `to_string`. The string is built at the same point and lives at least as long; no panic is added or removed (allocation failure aborts in both).
Classification: B
Assumptions: none.
Obligations: fork === upstream: the rewritten function behaves as the original on every input.
Evidence: an independent equivalence review by three reviewers, accepted on 2 of 3; summarised in formal/EXTRACTION-ISSUES.md.
Independent: yes

diff --git a/keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs b/keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs
--- a/keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs
+++ b/keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs
@@ -939,9 +939,9 @@
     /// user_<android user id>/<uid>_<prefix>_<alias>.
     fn make_blob_filename(&self, uid: AppUid, alias: &str, prefix: &str) -> PathBuf {
         let user = uid.owning_user();
-        let encoded_alias = Self::encode_alias(&format!("{prefix}_{alias}"));
+        let encoded_alias = Self::encode_alias(&{ let mut prefixed = prefix.to_owned(); prefixed.push_str("_"); prefixed.push_str(alias); prefixed });
         let mut path = self.make_user_path_name(user);
-        path.push(format!("{}_{}", uid.0, encoded_alias));
+        path.push({ let mut name = uid.0.to_string(); name.push_str("_"); name.push_str(&encoded_alias); name });
         path
     }
 
